{"id": "EUVD-2026-28769", "enisaUuid": "90d2a23f-b3ef-37b3-a3ac-df63d2811017", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc, afs: Fix missing error pointer check after rxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer()\n\nrxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer() can also return error pointers in addition to\nNULL, so just checking for NULL is not sufficient.\n\nFix this by:\n\n (1) Changing rxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer() to return -ENOMEM rather than NULL\n     on allocation failure.\n\n (2) Making the callers in afs use IS_ERR() and PTR_ERR() to pass on the\n     error code returned.", "datePublished": "2026-05-08T14:22:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d854c93b12f2076c564f595b41b93b02fd42a0f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d55fa7cd4b19ba91b34b307d769c149e56ad0a75", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54331c5dcc6d97683d7ca2788e7ef9c9505e1477", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4245a79003adf30e67f8e9060915bd05cb31d142"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qc73-3qqx-fc2q", "CVE-2026-43463"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0597cc82-6cc4-3f31-a580-ad56614ec3c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0b48cca8-7119-3d4f-a70e-099654a61363", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "543eeb47-005e-30d7-ad99-806cd201f2b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "72904d7b9bfbf2dd146254edea93958bc35bbbfe <4245a79003adf30e67f8e9060915bd05cb31d142"}, {"id": "5c179fed-468f-3434-ad3c-6d2f2efa243e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.9"}, {"id": "6678b477-459b-3c33-9a81-aa5e3769bbfb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.19"}, {"id": "a777f37d-c918-3e67-934e-3b0dbed012f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Lin